Drop MOVE's two eager allocations on the miss path (frankenredis-jvskj)

THE PREDICTION THIS TESTS. MOVE is my worst measured route and its own arm is the
unstable one -- 15% between 100-sample runs against redis's 1%, 12% outliers against
2% -- which is the allocator signature frankenlibc and frankentorch converged on
independently. Hoisting these allocations is behaviour-neutral, so if the variance AND
the gap both shrink the mechanism is confirmed; if only the variance moves, the gap is
elsewhere and this stops being the lead.

WHAT IT CHANGES. `key_owned`/`db_owned` were built EAGERLY on every MOVE -- including
a miss, which returns Integer(0) at the source-existence check far above -- solely so
the lazy builder closure could capture them. The closure then CLONED both, so an
invoked builder allocated four times for two values. `key` and `db_arg` are `&[u8]`
parameters that outlive the closure, so it borrows them and allocates once, only when
it runs. Miss path goes from two allocations to zero; upstream moveCommand on a miss
allocates nothing at all.

NOT COMPILED. /data is at the 42G floor and no build of any kind is permitted, so this
is verified structurally only: `git apply --check` rc=0. That is not a type check, and
I have had a structural check pass on a patch that then failed to build. The borrow
question is the one to watch -- the closure is passed to a `&mut self` method while
capturing two function parameters, which should be fine because neither borrows from
`self`, but "should" is doing work there.

SCOPED TO MOVE DELIBERATELY. Five other executors share the exact pattern --
zstore, zdiffstore, bitop (2 clones each), zinter, setstore (1 each) -- and the fix is
mechanical in all of them. I am not touching them here: MOVE is the one with a
measurement attached, and six uncompilable route changes is six times the risk of one.
Once this is confirmed on the clock, the other five are a follow-up with a known
answer.

APPLY WITH:
    git apply scripts/move_miss_alloc.patch
    python3 scripts/build_preflight.py        # must clear
    cargo check -p fr-runtime                 # THE step this patch has not had
    <full suite, then FR_SERVER_BIN=<a binary you built> for any measurement>

--- a/crates/fr-runtime/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/fr-runtime/src/lib.rs
@@ -16119,13 +16119,21 @@
